Our project is the World Vision UK website. It is a charity platform that helps people support children and communities through child sponsorship and donations.

The website allows users to explore sponsorship opportunities, learn about charitable activities, select donation amounts, and make contributions through available payment options.

From the frontend perspective, the project involves developing responsive user interfaces, implementing interactive forms, integrating APIs, handling user interactions, and ensuring a consistent experience across desktop and mobile devices.

My responsibilities include understanding business requirements, reviewing UI designs, developing reusable components, integrating backend APIs, fixing UI issues, and collaborating with the backend and QA teams.

We follow the development process from requirement analysis and implementation through testing, bug fixing, code review, and deployment. I would also like to walk you through the modules I handle, the current development status, and any ongoing tasks so we can align on priorities.




